---
import Default from "../layouts/Default.astro";
---

<Default
  title="Getting started"
  subtitle="Install, your first program, and the canonical commit-test-bench workflow."
>
  <article class="md-body">
    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>
      The SDK is a Go module. Pick the surface package(s) you need — they auto-pull
      <code>internal/*</code> through the workspace replace directives.
    </p>
    <pre is:raw><code>go get github.com/kitsunium/sdk/pkg/v1/logger
go get github.com/kitsunium/sdk/pkg/v1/codec
go get github.com/kitsunium/sdk/pkg/v1/errs</code></pre>

    <p>
      Module versions follow standard <code>vX.Y.Z</code> semver — <code>pkg/v1</code>
      is the only public surface and signatures freeze post-<code>v1.0.0</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Hello, world</h2>
    <p>
      A minimal program exercising both production domains (logger + codec) and the
      error introspection helpers:
    </p>
    <pre is:raw><code class="language-go">package main

import (
	&quot;fmt&quot;
	&quot;os&quot;

	logger &quot;github.com/kitsunium/sdk/pkg/v1/logger&quot;
	codec  &quot;github.com/kitsunium/sdk/pkg/v1/codec&quot;
	errs   &quot;github.com/kitsunium/sdk/pkg/v1/errs&quot;
)

type Greeting struct {
	Name    string `json:&quot;name&quot;`
	Message string `json:&quot;message&quot;`
}

func main() {
	// 1. Configure a text logger to stderr.
	log, err := logger.NewText(logger.Config{Writer: os.Stderr})
	if err != nil {
		fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, &quot;logger:&quot;, err)
		os.Exit(1)
	}

	// 2. Encode then decode the same struct through the codec facade —
	//    swap &quot;json&quot; for &quot;cbor&quot; / &quot;yaml&quot; / &quot;msgpack&quot; / &quot;base64&quot; without
	//    touching any other line.
	in := Greeting{Name: &quot;kitsune&quot;, Message: &quot;Bonjour&quot;}
	data, mErr := codec.Marshal(codec.JSON, in)
	if mErr != nil {
		log.Error(&quot;marshal failed&quot;,
			logger.String(&quot;reason&quot;, errs.ReasonOf(mErr)),
			logger.String(&quot;public&quot;, errs.PublicOf(mErr)))
		os.Exit(1)
	}

	var out Greeting
	if uErr := codec.Unmarshal(codec.JSON, data, &amp;out); uErr != nil {
		log.Error(&quot;unmarshal failed&quot;,
			logger.String(&quot;reason&quot;, errs.ReasonOf(uErr)))
		os.Exit(1)
	}

	log.Info(&quot;round-trip ok&quot;,
		logger.String(&quot;encoded&quot;, string(data)),
		logger.String(&quot;decoded&quot;, out.Message))
}</code></pre>

    <p>
      Run it and you'll see something like:
    </p>
    <pre is:raw><code>time=2026-05-22T09:00:00Z level=INFO msg=&quot;round-trip ok&quot; encoded=&quot;{\&quot;name\&quot;:\&quot;kitsune\&quot;,\&quot;message\&quot;:\&quot;Bonjour\&quot;}&quot; decoded=&quot;Bonjour&quot; framework_version=dev</code></pre>

    <h2>Swap the codec at runtime</h2>
    <p>
      Every Format is a string — pick from <code>codec.Available()</code> (returns
      18 names) or hard-code <code>codec.JSON</code> / <code>codec.CBOR</code> / <code>codec.YAML</code>
      / <code>codec.MsgPack</code> / <code>codec.TOML</code> / <code>codec.XML</code> / <code>codec.NDJSON</code>
      / <code>codec.PEM</code> / <code>codec.ASN1DER</code> / <code>codec.FlatBuffers</code> /
      <code>codec.TLV</code> / <code>codec.CSV</code> / the <code>baseenc</code> family
      (<code>codec.Base64</code> / <code>codec.Base64URL</code> / <code>codec.Base32</code> /
      <code>codec.Base16</code> / <code>codec.Hex</code> / <code>codec.Ascii85</code>). The
      <code>Marshal</code> / <code>Unmarshal</code> contract is identical for every one.
    </p>

    <h2>Working with errors</h2>
    <p>
      SDK errors are never raw <code>fmt.Errorf</code>. Every one carries a dotted-quad
      <code>Code</code> (e.g. <code>0.3.2.1</code> = JSON marshal failed), a screaming-snake
      <code>Reason</code> (<code>JSON_MARSHAL_FAILED</code>), a wire-safe <code>Public</code>,
      and a log-only <code>Private</code>. Match on Reason for UX-stable branching:
    </p>
    <pre is:raw><code class="language-go">if errs.HasReason(err, &quot;JSON_MARSHAL_FAILED&quot;) {
    // recover or fallback
}

code := errs.CodeOf(err)
if code.Layer() == 3 &amp;&amp; code.Package() == 2 {
    // came from internal/service/codec/json
}</code></pre>

    <h2>Canonical workflow</h2>
    <p>
      Everything goes through Bazel 9; <code>go test ./...</code> still works for quick
      local iteration, but CI only runs <code>bazel</code>.
    </p>
    <pre is:raw><code>make build    # mod tidy → gazelle → gofumpt → bazel build //...
make test     # bazel test --config=race //...
make lint     # drift assertion: gazelle diff + gofumpt -l + ktn-linter
make bench    # regenerate pkg/v1/codec/BENCH.md (15-25 min @ -benchtime=2s)
make docs     # rebuild this static site → docs/site/dist/</code></pre>

    <h2>Next steps</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Read the <a href="/philosophy/">9 SDK rules</a> before adding code.</li>
      <li>Skim the <a href="/architecture/">4-layer architecture</a> — every import direction is enforced by Bazel visibility.</li>
      <li>Browse the <a href="/adr/">six ADRs</a> for the load-bearing decisions.</li>
      <li>See the <a href="/benchmarks/">benchmarks</a> to pick the codec that fits your throughput / size budget.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
